/**
 * LUNG CANCER: THE UK AND NHS LAYER. Facts checked 2026-09-25 against the pages cited on each row.
 *
 * Lung cancer is the cancer the NHS has changed most in the last five years, and the one where the gap between
 * rich and poor is widest. What is here: the UK figures by nation with the stage split, the emergency
 * presentation share and the deprivation gradient, which is steeper in lung cancer than in any other common
 * cancer and is stated here with four separate national sources; the National Lung Cancer Audit's State of the
 * Nation 2026 with its headline findings and dates; the NHS route from the lung health check and the national
 * screening programme, through the NICE NG12 chest X-ray rules, the National Optimal Lung Cancer Pathway and
 * the 28, 31 and 62 day standards, to the lung multidisciplinary team, the thoracic surgery units, reflex
 * molecular testing and smoking cessation; every NICE decision on a lung cancer medicine read from
 * nice.org.uk, with the Scottish Medicines Consortium's and Wales's positions, including the refusals and the
 * terminated appraisals; the trials open in the UK with their sites; the UK trial legacy, which for lung cancer
 * is unusually large; UK researchers from their public pages; Roy Castle Lung Cancer Foundation and the other
 * charities; the costs and the benefits; and where the four nations differ, which for lung cancer is the
 * largest difference on any of these pages: England is running a national screening programme, Scotland
 * starts phase 1 in 2027/28, Wales expects its first invitations in 2027, and Northern Ireland has neither a
 * programme nor a pilot.
 *
 * No figure is remembered: each carries the page it was read from. Where a page could not be read, the gap is
 * named with the response the server gave.
 *
 * The record this keys to is `nsclc` (src/data/cancers.ts) while the lung taxonomy is being settled elsewhere;
 * `sclc` and the lung parent ids are aliases, so the page renders for either. This file adds Roy Castle Lung
 * Cancer Foundation, the two specialist heart and chest hospitals the corpus did not have, UK researchers from
 * their public pages, the legacy trial records and the `ukPathway`.
 */
